{"id": "EUVD-2026-102334", "enisaUuid": "ca81871c-befd-3026-bcda-6a5e69ad8c8e", "description": "Netgate pfSense CE through 2.9.0 contains a php.ini injection vulnerability that allows authenticated users with General Setup privileges to inject directives by submitting an unvalidated timezone value. Attackers can embed a quote and newline to add auto_prepend_file pointing at /var/db/zoneinfo, executing PHP as root after php.ini is regenerated at boot or php-fpm restart.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:46:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T01:08:42", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/abraxas/pfsense-timezone-phpini", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/pfsense-ce-leftovers", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/usr/local/www/system.php#L288", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/system.inc#L2377-L2380", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/rc.php_ini_setup#L163-L166", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/rc.php_ini_setup#L220", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netgate-pfsense-ce-through-2.9.0-php-ini-injection-via-timezone-setting"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111222", "GHSA-3c6h-8mvp-vqx3"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.96, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "246946b8-64d0-3f74-a6b7-639dbc487525", "product": {"name": "pfSense CE", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ad59fa9c-8dbf-31b3-b791-115baf33ffa0", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}], "isExploited": false}